    "source": "google_jobs",
    "description": "About Abbott\nAbbott is a global healthcare leader creating breakthrough science to improve people's health. We're always looking towards the future anticipating changes in medical science and technology.\n\n\n\nWorking at Abbott\nAt Abbott you can do work that matters, grow and learn, care for yourself and family, be your true self, and live a full life. You will have access to:\n\n\n\nCareer development with an international company where you can grow the career you dream of.\nA company recognized as a great place to work in dozens of countries around the world and named one of the most admired companies in the world by Fortune.\nA company that is recognized as one of the best big companies to work for as well as a best place to work for diversity, working mothers, female executives, and scientists.\n\n\nMedical Devices\nOur medical devices help more than 10,000 people have healthier hearts, improve quality of life for thousands of people living with chronic pain and movement disorders, and liberate more than 500,000 people with diabetes from routine fingersticks.\n\n\n\nAbout Diabetes Care\nWe're focused on helping people with diabetes manage their health with life-changing products that provide accurate data to drive better-informed decisions. We're revolutionizing the way people monitor their glucose levels with our new sensing technology.\n\n\n\nAbbott Diabetes Care (ADC) Division is looking for a Brand Manager Digital and Consumer based in UAE.\n\n\n\nAs Brand Manager you'll be responsible to:\nDrive, monitor, and control digital and consumer-related programs and activities to ensure Abbott's brand reputation, voice, perception, and image is safeguarded and represented in an optimal way. This includes driving brand awareness related campaigns and activations around the brand overall, specific programs, as well as existing and new product launches targeted for consumers in Gulf and Pakistan. This is all with the aim to help drive the business so that the organization's short and long-term business objectives are met. Comply with regulations and standards and protect the organization's public reputation.\n\n\n\nWhat You'll Do\n\nEnsure that all activities are performed in compliance with quality system requirements.\nLead the development and execution of integrated marketing/communications campaigns including collaborating and actively problem solving with cross-functional peers in PR, marketing, digital to ensure timely and strong execution as well as ensuring its alignment with the business objectives and goals.\nReview and monitor all ad-promo material to ensure the brand is effectively and accurately represented from a visual and messaging perspective together with close collaborations with regulatory to ensure alignment to policies and procedures.\nDirect and manage the execution of the various brand related projects and campaigns along with ensuring clear KPIs are set for each.\nSet and drive internal and external communication programs to create awareness and drive engagement with our brand and products including online/offline channels.\nCraft and create content and promotional material/templates to be used in both online and offline channels such as brochures, flyers, invitations, agendas, giveaways, e-newsletters, whitepapers, customer testimonials, videos, etc.\nClose collaboration with the different functional team members to ensure alignment on new material being created, objectives, channels to use, target audiences, and amplification targets.\nEnsure our brand is effectively represented on various online/digital channels such as our websites, LinkedIn, partners’ websites, etc.\nManage our media plan for our promotional campaigns (online and offline publications and channels).\nEnsure clear metrics and KPIs are set in place for the various promotional/advertisement campaigns.\nPerformance monitoring and analytics on all various campaigns, events, advertising, and content marketing activities (customer engagement, conversion, reach, shares, likes, brand awareness, etc.).\nOversee appropriate agency relationships and program work in support of strategy.\nDrive innovative CRM campaigns to continuously engage both new and existing consumers and healthcare professionals.\n\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\nA minimum of a bachelor's degree is required and MBA or advanced degree is preferred in Business Management, Marketing Communications, or Digital Marketing.\nEmail marketing (marketing automation) software.\nMicrosoft Office suite (Word, PowerPoint, Outlook).\nData analytics tools (Excel, Tableau).\nGood understanding of digital channels (web, social, advertising).\nKnowledge of SEO and Google Analytics.\nEnglish excellence is a must.\n20% travel required.\nProven work experience of at least 8 years in digital and social marketing communication.\nKnowledge of social trends and marketing strategies.\nFamiliarity with B2C advertising campaigns.\nHands-on experience with web content management tools.\nExperience with marketing campaigns and social media.\nProject management skills such as PMP or other certifications is preferred.\nAnalytical skills: ability to consume, identify, and act on data.\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills.\nResourceful, self-motivated, eager learner, good organizational skills, detail-oriented, ability to prioritize, team-player, and honors deadlines.\n\n\nFollow your career aspirations to Abbott for diverse opportunities with a company that provides the growth and strength to build your future. Abbott is an equal opportunity employer committed to employee diversity.",
