    "source": "google_jobs",
    "description": "Galderma is the emerging pure-play dermatology category leader, present in approximately 90 countries. We deliver an innovative, science-based portfolio of premium flagship brands and services that span the full spectrum of the fast-growing dermatology market through Injectable Aesthetics, Dermatological Skincare and Therapeutic Dermatology. Since our foundation in 1981, we have dedicated our focus and passion to the human body's largest organ - the skin - meeting individual consumer and patient needs with superior outcomes in partnership with healthcare professionals. Because we understand that the skin, we are in shapes our lives, we are advancing dermatology for every skin story. We look for people who focus on getting results, embrace learning and bring a positive energy. They must combine initiative with a sense of teamwork and collaboration. Above all, they must be passionate about doing something meaningful for consumers, patients, and the healthcare professionals we serve every day. We aim to empower each employee and promote their personal growth while ensuring business needs are met now and into the future. Across our company, we embrace diversity and respect the dignity, privacy, and personal rights of every employee. At Galderma, we actively give our teams reasons to believe in our bold ambition to become the leading dermatology company in the world. With us, you have the ultimate opportunity to gain new and challenging work experiences and create an unparalleled, direct impact. Job Title : Key Account Manager Biologics Localisation : Abu Dhabi The Key Account Manager – Biologics is responsible for developing, managing, and growing strategic partnerships with key healthcare accounts to optimize sales and revenue opportunities across the Galderma portfolio. The role focuses on building long-term, value-based relationships with key stakeholders, identifying growth opportunities within accounts, and ensuring the successful implementation of strategic account plans. The Key Account Manager collaborates cross-functionally to deliver integrated solutions that enhance patient access, strengthen customer partnerships, and support the company’s broader commercial objectives within the biologics and dermatology space. Responsabilities Key Account Strategy & Development Develop and continuously strengthen strategic relationships with key healthcare accounts to support the company’s vision and drive portfolio growth. Build and implement strategic account plans aligned with business objectives to maximize account potential and long-term value. Lead the development and execution of Joint Business Plans with priority accounts to create mutually beneficial partnerships. Identify opportunities to expand collaboration within accounts and enhance portfolio adoption. Account Management & Business Growth Achieve and exceed assigned sales targets, business objectives, and performance KPIs. Manage Tier 1 and Tier 2 accounts, building long-term partnerships with key customers and healthcare institutions. Analyze account performance through regular reviews of sales data, market trends, and forecasts to identify opportunities for growth and improved efficiency. Gather competitive intelligence and market insights to support strategic planning and enhance account performance. Patient Journey & Stakeholder Engagement Map the patient journey within key accounts to identify barriers and opportunities to improve patient access and outcomes. Identify and engage key decision-makers, influencers, and stakeholders within accounts. Develop comprehensive stakeholder mapping and engagement strategies to strengthen partnerships and drive value creation. Cross-Functional Collaboration Lead cross-functional collaboration across Sales, Medical, Marketing, Market Access, Training, Supply Chain, Finance, and other enabling functions to support account strategy execution. Act as the central point of coordination to ensure a unified “One Gal