    "description": "Job Title: Retail Marketing & Production Specialist\n\nDepartment: Retail Marketing\n\n Reports To: Retail Marketing Manager\n\n Location: GCC / Middle East\n\n\n\n\nJob Purpose\n\nTo manage retail marketing materials, fixtures production, and in-store branding execution across key retail channels.\n\nThe role ensures high-quality implementation of POSM, stands, and Shop-in-Shop (SIS) projects while maintaining cost control, timeline adherence, and ROI visibility.\n\nThis position bridges Marketing, Sales, and Suppliers to ensure retail excellence on the ground.\n\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nRetail Display & Fixture Production Management\n\nManage production of stands, SIS, lightboxes, signboards, and other retail fixtures.Coordinate with production vendors for design, material selection, and costing.Review technical drawings and ensure specifications match retail standards.Supervise fabrication quality and ensure brand consistency.Conduct pre-installation and post-installation inspections.\n\n\nPOSM & Branding Material Management\n\nPlan and execute POSM production (wobblers, posters, shelf strips, danglers, etc.).Ensure correct placement and visibility in stores.Monitor material durability and replacement cycles.Maintain a database of materials per store and per campaign.Ensure alignment with brand guidelines and global standards.\n\n\nRetail Expansion & SIS Implementation\n\nSupport new store openings and retail expansion projects.Coordinate layout planning for new SIS installations.Work with landlords and retailers for approvals (where needed).Ensure on-time execution of installation projects.Track expansion costs vs. approved budget.\n\n\nBudget & Cost Control (OBM / A&P / Retail Investment)\n\nTrack production and installation expenses.Ensure cost optimization without compromising quality.Monitor ROI of retail investments.Prepare retail investment reports for management and HQ.Manage vendor quotations and negotiation process.\n\n\nRetail