    "description": "Description\nOxford Nanopore Technologies is headquartered at the Oxford Science Park outside Oxford UK with satellite offices and a commercial presence in many global locations across the US, APAC, and Europe.\n\n\nOxford Nanopore employs from multiple subject areas including nanopore science, molecular biology and applications, informatics, engineering, electronics, manufacturing, and commercialisation. The management team led by CEO Dr Gordon Sanghera has a track record of delivering disruptive technologies to the market.\n\n\nOxford Nanopore's sequencing platform is the only technology that offers real-time analysis in fully scalable formats from pocket to population scale that can analyse native DNA or RNA and sequence any length of fragment to achieve short to ultra-long read lengths. Our goal is to enable the analysis of any living thing by anyone anywhere!\n\n\nIn this role you will be responsible for developing, managing, and implementing the regional marketing strategy in the MEAI (Middle East, Africa, India) region. This role will also provide support to facilitate and enable the channel partners across the EMEAI region (including Eastern Europe) to help reach the company's revenue goals and translate market insights and product knowledge into competitive strategies and tactics.\n\n\nThe marketing lead will work closely with their marketing and commercial colleagues to ensure alignment of focus areas to support the region's commercial goals. You will monitor the overall performance of the marketing activities in the assigned territories in the region in line with the company's global strategic priorities and business growth as the need arises.\n\n\nThe details\nThe ideal candidate for this position will have a solid understanding of the genomics market in the region with demonstrated success in developing product market strategies both short and medium term including planning and executing of regional strategies and growing market penetration.\n\n\nKey responsibilities include but are not limited to:\n\nUsing regional market knowledge and customer insights develop and implement comprehensive marketing strategies for the MEAI region and channel partners that are translated to operational plans in the assigned territories focusing on growing sales and increasing profitability aligned to the company's strategic priorities.\nWork with regional commercial leaders, drive and monitor channel partners performance across the EMEAI (including Eastern Europe) region. Pilot, incubate, iterate profitable local programs/initiatives and implement global marketing/commercial marketing programs in the region.\nUse regional market knowledge and customer insights to articulate regional marketing strategies and identify the region's market growth opportunities to reach local vital customer segments including the delivery of the global messaging and local deployment plans across the MEAI region and EMEAI channel partner territories.\nUnderstand the regional market trends, short- and longer-term opportunities for our technology and products, build marketing strategies and plans aligned with the central marketing team.\nA key element of the role will be collecting, evaluating, reacting to and communicating field information and communicating customer feedback to global strategy and roadmap as well as commercial goals and objectives.\nWith the marketing operations and events team, help build the tactical plan and play an active role in the deployment of the plan. Measure, review and iterate for best practice against critical metrics.\nSetting, communicating and maintaining timelines and priorities including expectation management on multiple projects.\nAny other duties as might be required within the remit and responsibilities of the post.\n\nWhat we're looking for...\n\nBachelor's degree or equivalent experience in Life Sciences, Business or Marketing.\nProven experience in marketing, demonstrable experience in develop