quirements**\n\n* Proven experience (5\\+ years) in corporate communications, public affairs, CSR, or reputation management within multinational environments.\n* Strong understanding of media ecosystems, corporate positioning, brand reputation, and modern communications practices.\n* Experience developing CSR strategies and executing multi\\-market social impact programs.\n* Demonstrated ability to lead crisis communication responses.\n* Experience managing PR agencies and external partners globally.\n* Strong executive communication skills, with the ability to coach and prepare leaders for high‑visibility engagements.\n* Ability to serve as corporate spokesperson, or to identify and groom a spokesperson in the future.\n* Hands on approach bundled with strategic thinking when needed\n* High comfort working with ambiguity and building functions from the ground up.\n* Demonstrated resilience and adaptability in environments characterised by change.\n* Excellent stakeholder management and relationship‑building skills.\n* Strong writing, storytelling, and editorial judgement abilities.\n\n**Personal Attributes**\n\n* Purpose‑driven mindset, committed to meaningful social and community impact.\n* Confident, composed, and proactive communicator.\n* Entrepreneurial spirit with a builder mindset.\n* Collaborative leadership style and the ability to galvanise cross‑functional teams.\n* High integrity, sound judgement, and a reputation for trustworthiness\n\n  \n\n**Additional Information**  \n\nWe believe in fairly compensating all our people by providing them with a world\\-class health insurance plan and a range of both core benefits and flex benefits for individual preferences. You will receive:\n\n* Hybrid Working Policy\n* Discretionary performance related bonus\n* Personalized Flex\\-Benefits\n* A focus on your wellbeing, including talks and access to self\\-development tools.\n* Medical insurance for employees.\n* Comprehensive leave package of 40 days inclusive of Pu