s, founder profiles, or event opportunities\n* Strong instinct for messaging, tone, and how to position a company credibly in public\n* Ability to manage multiple communication threads without losing clarity or detail\n* Good judgment on what is newsworthy, what is brand\\-safe, and what should be deprioritised\n\n### **Market \\& Brand Understanding**\n\n\n* Strong understanding of financial markets, startup narratives, and ideally Web3 / tokenisation / fintech environments\n* Ability to turn market developments into timely and relevant communications angles\n* Strong understanding of branding and positioning, able to tell the difference between narrative\\-building and noise\n* Sensitivity to institutional tone, reputation, and audience context\n\n### **Execution \\& Working Style**\n\n\n* Organised, detail\\-oriented, and strong in follow\\-through\n* Able to work independently and maintain momentum across outreach and communications workflows\n* High ownership, low ego, and comfortable with feedback\n* Comfortable operating in a startup environment where speed matters but quality is maintained\n* Able to communicate clearly with founders, media contacts, and external stakeholders\n\n**Nice to Have**\n----------------\n\n\n* Experience in RWAs, real estate, tokenisation, crypto, fintech, or regulated sectors\n* Existing relationships with media or event organisers in relevant industries\n* Experience working with founders, executives, or C\\-level spokespeople\n* Experience managing PR agencies or external communications vendors\n* Familiarity with LinkedIn thought leadership, bylines, or op\\-ed placement workflows\n\n**What Success Looks Like**\n---------------------------\n\n\n* OneAsset's public narrative becomes more consistent, credible, and recognisable\n* Media and event outreach becomes more proactive and structured\n* Founder profiling improves and speaking opportunities become more targeted\n* Press releases, pitches, and messaging assets are well\\-wr