ement measurement framework: define best practices based on results and create a culture of sharing best-in-class frameworks and driving continuous improvement.\n• Define buyer segments: identify key buyer segments in the marketplace (beyond industry affiliation) and group users/clients by behavioral data for more efficient and effective targeting.\n• Collaborate with B2B CoE, digital marketing, and sales excellence to deploy technology infrastructure for B2B marketing including CRM system to manage relationships more effectively, CDP for greater personalization, etc.\n• The head of B2B marketing will serve as a key strategic and operating partner to the product, value-added services, and commercial and money movement solutions business units.\n• Developing B2B marketing strategy: help build demand and drive adoption and retention for new and existing Visa B2B products across all stages of usage.\n• Product lifecycle: align Visa’s marketing efforts (promotions and sales) with Visa’s product lifecycle stages, i.e., development, introduction, growth, maturity, saturation, and decline.\n• Build messaging and positioning for products and services including unique value propositions, product narratives, solutions bundling.\n• Connect to other parts of regional marketing, product integration, and marketing through sponsorships.\n• Lead collaborative interactions with key stakeholders across the different business units.\n• This is a hybrid position. Expectation of days in office will be confirmed by your hiring manager.\n\nQualifications:\n\nBasic qualifications:\n\n12 or more years of work experience with a bachelor’s degree or at least 10 years of work experience with an advanced degree (e.g. masters/MBA/JD/MD) or a minimum of 5 years of work experience with a PhD.\n\nPreferred qualifications:\n• 12–15 years of experience with an advanced degree (e.g. masters, MBA).\n• Experience as head of B2B marketing for a multiproduct organization at scale.\n• Leader who understand