    "description": "This is where you save and sustain lives\nAt Baxter we are deeply connected by our mission. No matter your role at Baxter, your work makes a positive impact on people around the world. You'll feel a sense of purpose throughout the organization as we know our work improves outcomes for millions of patients.\n\n\nBaxter's products and therapies are found in almost every hospital worldwide, in clinics and in the home. For over 85 years we have pioneered significant medical innovations that transform healthcare.\n\n\nTogether we create a place where we are happy, successful and inspire each other. This is where you can do your best work.\n\n\nJoin us at the intersection of saving and sustaining lives where your purpose accelerates our mission.\n\n\nRole overview\nThe Project Manager MEA Kidney Care will oversee and drive strategic commercial projects across the MEA region including expansion into new markets, optimization of existing operations and execution of new business models. This role is critical to ensuring the growth and success of Baxter Kidney Care MEA focusing on strategic distributor relationships, digital transformation and the expansion of PD & Acute Therapies. The Project Manager will work closely with the EMEA team to align and execute these initiatives contributing significantly to the company's growth target in the region.\n\n\nStrategic project management\n\n  Lead and manage major commercial projects such as Libya, North Africa, South Africa and Iraq expansions ensuring alignment with the company's strategic goals.\n  Develop and maintain detailed project plans including timelines, resource allocation and budget management.\n  Identify and mitigate project risks ensuring timely and successful delivery of objectives.\n\nDigital transformation\n\n  Utilize and promote the adoption of digital PD products and tools to enhance customer relationship management.\n  Lead digital marketing initiatives to support the expansion of PD & Acute Therapies and increase market penetration.\n\nMarket expansion & portfolio management\n\n  Focus on the expansion of PD & Acute Therapies, identifying major opportunities annually for market or portfolio expansion.\n  Leverage Vantive in the region to optimize product and country portfolios.\n  Manage investments with a focus on high ROI, cost control and efficient use of digital tools.\n\nGeox (Geographical expansion)\n\n  Work and coordinate with MEA and EMEA Geox teams on the rollout of Geox projects in the MEA region.\n  Track launch, implementation and sales performance of all Geox activities.\n\nCross-functional collaboration & communication\n\n  Foster a One Team MEA culture working closely with the EMEA team to align strategies and execute projects effectively.\n  Lead and coordinate communication efforts across different channels to ensure transparency and engagement.\n  Act as a liaison between MEA and EMEA teams ensuring alignment on critical issues and projects.\n\nFinancial management & reporting\n\n  Monitor and report on financial performance including sales, operating income and OPEX ensuring alignment with financial targets for the designated projects.\n  Provide regular updates on project progress and financial performance highlighting key achievements and areas for improvement.\n\nInnovation & learning\n\n  Encourage innovative thinking and the development of new ideas to improve processes and outcomes.\n  Promote a culture of feedback, learning and continuous improvement within the team.\n  Empower team members through education and training, fostering a learning organization.\n\nEducation\nBachelor's degree in Business Administration, Project Management or a related field. A master's degree is preferred.\n\n\nExperience\n\n  Minimum of 5 to 7 years of experience in project management, particularly in the healthcare or medical devices industry in MEA region.\n  Proven experience in managing large-scale commercial projects with a significant fin