    "description": "We are hiring a director of ecommerce for MEA & APAC region\nAs the ecommerce director MEA & APAC, you will play a pivotal role in driving digital sales and optimizing the e-commerce experience for Ennismore's diverse brand portfolio. The scope of properties will include all Lifestyle Collective properties in the MEA and APAC regions. You will be responsible for spearheading initiatives to increase direct bookings on our brand websites, working in close partnership with product, revenue, and property teams. With a focus on operational leadership, digital marketing, and revenue management, you will ensure that our digital platforms deliver a seamless, high-converting, and commercially impactful user experience.\n\n\n\nKey responsibilities:\n\n  Optimize website performance: Collaborate with product, revenue, and brand VPs to enhance websites and booking engine functionality, user experience, and conversion rates. Leverage insights from the product team to continuously refine digital touchpoints and maximize performance.\n  Deep product partnership: Work hand-in-hand with the product team to ensure alignment between commercial objectives and product development. Prioritize enhancements and features that drive direct bookings, user engagement, and overall website effectiveness.\n  Lead acquisition marketing: Manage the acquisition marketing strategy and paid campaigns with direct oversight of the digital marketing and regional e-commerce teams. Develop digital marketing campaigns that effectively drive traffic and convert into direct bookings.\n  Coordinate paid media & ROI: Oversee paid media investments, ensuring a focus on budget efficiency and maximizing returns. Drive media teams and performance improvements. Collaborate with brand team on CRM campaigns. The ecommerce director will also drive the campaign calendar in collaboration with the brand teams.\n  Performance assessment: Partner with the data and insights team to assess website performa